action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P72: does the mesh view draw ONLY when it is asked to?
#
# Coordinates are origin=frame, read off testapp/output/screenshots/
# P72-taller-20260919-213420.png, a 520x808 capture of a 520x780 window -- so
# 1x, and the 28px difference is the title bar the frame origin includes.
#
# RE-MEASURED after the mesh view was narrowed from 440x300 to 340x240 points,
# which it had to be: at 440 plus 20 of padding each side the column was wider
# than a 440-point phone and iOS clipped both edges of every line. That moved
# this row 30px up, from y 541 to y 511, and the old coordinates would have
# clicked the line below. A file measured against one build is not a file
# measured against the next one.
#
# RE-MEASURED AGAIN when "Auto spin" was added as a third button: x moved from
# 75/191 to 190/305 while y stayed at 511. Twice in one day, which is the
# argument for the note above rather than against it.
#
# **The four key rows need no coordinates, which is the one pleasant thing about
# them.** A key goes to the first responder, and AppKitBackend's key target makes
# itself first responder when the window becomes key. So these rows cannot be
# invalidated by a layout change, and they are last so nothing after them can be.
#
# They assert four things, and two of them were failing until 2026-09-19:
#
#   KEY 1 'U+F700' shift=no  step 0.1  height 1.40
#   MODIFIERS down shift=true          <- a modifier alone, with no key
#   KEY 2 'U+F700' shift=yes step 1.0  height 2.40
#   MODIFIERS up shift=false
#
# The U+F700 was U+001E before the synthesiser was fixed, so the arrow matched
# nothing and the height never moved; and the last line said shift=TRUE, because
# the synthesiser released the modifier after building the event rather than
# before. Both are fixed in AppKitSynthesiser and both are recorded there.
#
# AND A SEVENTH TIME, when the window grew from 660 to 780 points. It had to:
# with the key readout added the content no longer fitted, and the title was
# clipped at the top of the window -- reported by a person looking at it, not by
# anything here. Nothing in this tree measures whether an app's own text is cut
# off, which is worth knowing given how much of this file is about measurement.
#
# AND A SIXTH TIME, after a fixed 400x640 frame was put around the column and
# then taken off again. The frame was an attempt to stop the column moving; it
# did not fix what it was aimed at (on iOS only the first tap after launch lands,
# whatever the layout does) and it moved every coordinate on both platforms, so
# it was removed. The column is narrower than the 520-point window and centred,
# which is why x is 69 here rather than the 20 of the padding.
#
# AND A FIFTH TIME when scroll arrived: the two readout lines it added moved the
# first row from 478 to 467 and the second from 507 to 496, and the mesh view's
# centre from y 242 to 235.
#
# **The fifth re-measurement found a defect rather than just a number.** The
# scroll readout was first written as one sentence that grew from `last: none`
# to `last: dy 8.4 precise, distance 2.06` the moment a scroll arrived. On iOS
# that wrapped to a second line MID-REPLAY, every row below moved up, and the
# four clicks this file makes after the scroll all missed -- silently, since a
# click on nothing reports nothing. The readouts are fixed-width now. A test app
# whose layout changes while its own action file runs invalidates the file.
#
# AND A FOURTH TIME when "Snapshot" joined "Export .glb" on the second row and
# a "snapshot:" readout line was added under it: the first row went from y 483
# to y 481 and the second from 511 to 510. Small, and still enough to miss a
# 20-point button if it had gone the other way.
#
# AND A THIRD TIME when "Export .glb" was added as a row BELOW this one. That
# was expected to change nothing here and it moved this row from y 511 to
# y 483: the window is a fixed 660 points and the content is centred in it, so
# an extra row lifts everything by half a row. Three re-measurements in one
# day, one of which contradicted the reasoning that said it was unnecessary.
#
# **The cube turning is not what this file tests.** That is read from two
# captures a second apart, which needs no input at all. What needs input is the
# opposite question: with the clock STOPPED, does the frame count stay put?
#
# `MTKView` defaults to driving itself at 60 Hz. `Mesh3DMetalView` sets
# `enableSetNeedsDisplay = true` so that the framework's `FrameClocks` is the
# only thing that makes it draw. If that line were deleted, every other piece of
# evidence in this app would look exactly the same -- the cube would turn, the
# count would climb, two captures would differ -- and the renderer would be
# burning a GPU on a still picture in every app that ever shows a mesh. This
# file is the only thing here that would notice.
#
# **The line is named from a measurement, not from memory.** Deleting
# `isPaused = true` was tried first, on the assumption that it was the one doing
# the work; the count still moved by 1 and the file still passed.
# `enableSetNeedsDisplay = true` makes the view ignore `isPaused` entirely.
# Deleting THAT gave 90, which is 1.5 seconds at 60 Hz. Both runs are on record
# in the note at that line.
#
# **The export is the FIRST click, and the order is the assertion.** "Auto spin"
# sets the rotation back to zero, so exporting after it would write a file whose
# node rotation is the identity -- which is exactly what an exporter that
# silently dropped `Mesh3DTransform` would also write. Exporting while the cube
# is visibly turned means the angle in the file can be read back and compared
# against nothing-happened. Checked with three.js's own GLTFLoader, not with a
# reader written here: a hand-written reader would agree with a hand-written
# writer about anything they both got wrong.
#
# Expected in testapp/p72-debug-events.log:
#
#   SCROLL 1 dy 80.00 dx -0.00 notched distance 3.400 -> 2.600
#   SCROLL 2 dy -80.00 dx -0.00 notched distance 2.600 -> 3.400
#   SNAPSHOT <w>x<h> px, <n> distinct colours, centre pixel <r,g,b>
#   SNAPSHOT PNG <n> bytes to <path>
#   EXPORTED <n> bytes to <path>
#   AUTO SPIN off
#   STOPPED at frame N
#   CHECK at frame M, D since the stop
#
# and the snapshot must report MORE THAN ONE distinct colour with a centre
# pixel that is a face colour, not the background. That is the assertion SoftPCB
# `plan.md` §10.7 says cannot be made: a window screenshot shows the app whatever
# the MTKView drew, so it passes either way. Measured both ways on 2026-09-19 --
# with the cube: 3 colours, centre 222,163,45 (the orange +X face shaded). With
# `meshes: []` and nothing else changed: 1 colour, centre 20,23,33, which is the
# background 0.08/0.09/0.13 exactly.
#
# **The two scroll rows assert three things at once and the pointer move is part
# of the assertion.** A scroll goes to whatever is under the pointer, so the
# `move` is what aims it at the mesh view rather than at the text below. dy +80
# is five notches at the 16 points per line AppKitBackend applies; `notched`
# rather than `precise` is the wheel being told apart from a trackpad; and the
# distance returning to exactly 3.400 is the sign convention holding in both
# directions rather than the value merely changing.
#
# Checked that it can fail: the same file with the `move` aimed at y 660 -- the
# text under the buttons -- reports ZERO scroll lines. The events are reaching
# the view because it is under the pointer, not because something is catching
# them window-wide.
#
# with D a small number. Each button press commits the view, and a commit hands
# the view a scene and asks for one frame. Measured here on 2026-09-19: D = 1 on
# AppKit, and 3 on UIKit, where a tap also puts the button through touch-down
# and touch-up. Anything near 90 (1.5 seconds at 60 Hz) is the free-running
# case, and that is the only outcome this file calls a failure -- a threshold
# tight enough to separate 1 from 3 would be asserting how many states a press
# goes through, which is not what is being tested.
#
# P72:這個 mesh view 是否**只在被要求時**才繪製?
#
# 座標為 origin=frame,量自 testapp/output/screenshots/P72-measure3-20260919-181212.png
# ——一張 520x808 的擷圖、對應 520x780 的視窗,因此是 1x,而那 28 像素的差是 frame 原點所含的標題列。
#
# 這是在 mesh view 由 440x300 點縮為 340x240 點之後**重新量過**的——而那非縮不可:440 加上左右各 20 的
# padding,整欄會比一支 440 點寬的手機還寬,於是 iOS 把每一行的兩側都切掉了。那讓這一列上移 30 像素,
# 由 y 541 變成 y 511,而舊座標會點到下面那一行。對著某一次建置量出來的檔案,不是對著下一次建置量的。
#
# **那四列按鍵不需要座標,而那是它們唯一令人愉快的地方。** 一個按鍵會送到 first responder,而
# AppKitBackend 的按鍵 target 會在 window 成為 key 時讓自己成為 first responder。因此這幾列不會被任何
# 版面變動作廢;而它們排在最後,所以也沒有東西會被它們影響。
#
# 它們斷言四件事,而其中兩件在 2026-09-19 之前是壞的(內容見上方英文區塊)。修好之前:U+F700 是 U+001E,
# 因此方向鍵什麼都對不上、高度從來沒動過;而最後一行寫的是 shift=TRUE,因為 synthesiser 是在建構事件
# **之後**才釋放修飾鍵、而不是之前。兩者都已在 AppKitSynthesiser 修正,也都記在該處。
#
# **第七次重新量測**發生在視窗由 660 點加高到 780 點時。非加不可:加上按鍵讀數之後內容已經放不下,
# 標題在視窗頂端被切掉——那是**由人看出來的**,不是這裡任何東西量出來的。這棵樹沒有任何機制會去量
# 「一支 app 自己的文字有沒有被切掉」,而考慮到這份檔案有多大篇幅在談量測,那件事值得知道。
#
# **第五次重新量測**發生在捲動加入時:它多出的兩行讀數,把第一列由 478 移到 467、第二列由 507 移到 496,
# 而 mesh view 的中心由 y 242 移到 235。
#
# **第五次重量測找到的是一個缺陷,不只是一個數字。** 捲動的讀數原本寫成一個句子,會在第一個捲動到達的
# 瞬間,由 `last: none` 長成 `last: dy 8.4 precise, distance 2.06`。在 iOS 上那會**在重放途中**換行成兩行,
# 底下每一列都往上移,而這份檔案在捲動之後的四次點擊全部落空——而且是靜默落空,因為點在空處不會回報任何事。
# 現在那些讀數已改為固定寬度。一支「在自己的動作檔執行途中改變版面」的測試 app,會讓那份檔案作廢。
#
# 在「Auto spin」作為第三個按鈕加入時**再一次重新量過**:x 由 75/191 變成 190/305,y 仍然是 511。
# 一天之內兩次——那是支持上面那段註記的理由,不是反對它的理由。
#
# **而在「Export .glb」作為這一列的下一列加入時,又量了第三次。** 原本預期那不會改到這裡的任何東西,
# 結果它把這一列由 y 511 移到 y 483:視窗固定 660 點、內容在其中置中,因此多一列會把所有東西往上抬半列。
# 一天之內三次重新量測,其中一次推翻了「不必量」的那個推理。
#
# **立方體會不會轉,不是這份檔案在測的東西。** 那是從相隔一秒的兩張擷圖讀出來的,根本不需要輸入。
# 需要輸入的是相反的那個問題:在時鐘**停掉**之後,幀計數會不會停住?
#
# `MTKView` 預設會自己以 60 Hz 驅動自己。`Mesh3DMetalView` 設了 `enableSetNeedsDisplay = true`,
# 好讓框架的 `FrameClocks` 成為唯一讓它繪製的東西。若那一行被刪掉,本 app 中其他每一項證據看起來都會
# 一模一樣——立方體會轉、計數會爬、兩張擷圖會不同——而那個 renderer 會在每一支顯示 mesh 的 app 裡,
# 為了一張靜止畫面燒掉一顆 GPU。此處只有這份檔案會發覺。
#
# **那一行是量出來的,不是憑印象寫的。** 一開始刪的是 `isPaused = true`,以為起作用的是它;結果計數
# 仍然只動了 1,這份檔案照樣通過。`enableSetNeedsDisplay = true` 會讓這個 view 完全忽略 `isPaused`。
# 刪掉**那一行**才得到 90——也就是 1.5 秒乘以 60 Hz。兩次執行都記在該行的註解裡。
#
# **匯出是第一次點擊,而那個順序就是斷言本身。** 「Auto spin」會把旋轉歸零,因此在它之後匯出,寫出的檔案
# 其 node 旋轉會是單位四元數——而那恰恰也是一個「靜默地把 `Mesh3DTransform` 丟掉」的匯出器會寫出來的東西。
# 在立方體明顯轉過去的時候匯出,才能把檔案裡的角度讀回來、與「什麼都沒發生」作比較。驗證用的是 three.js
# 自己的 GLTFLoader,而不是在這裡寫一個 reader:手寫的 reader 會在「兩邊都弄錯的地方」與手寫的 writer
# 取得一致。
#
# 預期出現在 testapp/p72-debug-events.log:
#
#   STOPPED at frame N
#   CHECK at frame M, D since the stop
#
# 而快照必須回報**多於一種**相異顏色,且中心像素是某個面的顏色、不是背景。那正是 SoftPCB `plan.md`
# §10.7 說「做不到」的那個斷言:一張視窗截圖不論那個 MTKView 畫了什麼都拍得到那支 app,因此兩種情況它
# 都會通過。2026-09-19 兩種都量過——有立方體時:3 種顏色、中心 222,163,45(受光的橘色 +X 面);把
# `meshes:` 改成 `[]`、其餘不動時:1 種顏色、中心 20,23,33,正好就是背景色 0.08/0.09/0.13。
#
# **那兩列 scroll 一次斷言三件事,而那個 move 是斷言的一部分。** 捲動會送到指標底下的東西,因此那個
# `move` 才是把它瞄準 mesh view、而不是瞄準下方文字的原因。dy +80 是五格滾輪乘以 AppKitBackend 所採用的
# 「每行 16 點」;回報 `notched` 而非 `precise`,是滾輪被與觸控板分辨開來;而距離**精確地**回到 3.400,
# 是那個符號約定在兩個方向上都成立——而不只是「數值有變」。
#
# 已查證它會失敗:同一份檔案把 `move` 瞄準 y 660(按鈕下方的文字)時,SCROLL 的行數是**零**。那些事件
# 之所以到得了那個 view,是因為它在指標底下,而不是因為有什麼東西在整個視窗範圍內攔截它們。
#
# 而 D 是一個小數字。每一次按鈕按下都會使 view commit,而一次 commit 會把場景交給 view 並要求一幀。
# 2026-09-19 在此實測:AppKit 的 D = 1、UIKit 的 D = 3(在 UIKit 上,一次點擊還會讓按鈕經過
# touch-down 與 touch-up)。接近 90(1.5 秒 x 60 Hz)的任何數字才是那個自由奔跑的情況,而那也是這份
# 檔案唯一視為失敗的結果——一個嚴到能區分 1 與 3 的門檻,斷言的會是「一次按下經過幾個狀態」,
# 而那不是此處要測的東西。
sleep,,,,,,2000000,let the clock run so the count is plainly moving first,macos
move,239,284,frame,,,,put the pointer over the mesh view -- a scroll goes where the pointer is,macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
scroll,0,5,,,,,five notches down: dy +80 and the camera must come CLOSER,macos
sleep,,,,,,400000,,macos
scroll,0,-5,,,,,and five back up: dy -80 and the distance must return,macos
sleep,,,,,,400000,,macos
click,113,547,frame,left,,,"Export .glb FIRST -- while the cube is still turned; see the note",macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
click,210,547,frame,left,,,"Snapshot -- reads the mesh view's own pixels back; see the note",macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
click,120,518,frame,left,,,"Auto spin -- writes AUTO SPIN off; the orbit must keep going",macos
sleep,,,,,,1000000,long enough for a capture to show the camera still moving,macos
click,238,518,frame,left,,,"Stop the clock -- writes STOPPED at frame N",macos
sleep,,,,,,1500000,"1.5s of nothing: 90 frames if the view drives itself",macos
click,354,518,frame,left,,,"Check again -- writes CHECK at frame M and the delta",macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,let the readout settle before the capture,macos
key,,,,,upArrow,,plain Up -- height must rise by 0.1 and the key must be U+F700,macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
keydown,,,,,shift,,"hold Shift -- MODIFIERS down shift=true, with NO key",macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
key,,,,,upArrow,,Shift-Up -- the step must be 1.0 rather than 0.1,macos
sleep,,,,,,300000,,macos
keyup,,,,,shift,,release -- MODIFIERS up shift=false,macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
